<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142d4c"><meta name="description" content="Explore assistance programs available in Maryland."><title>Maryland Assistance Programs — American Aid Network</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/google-analytics.php"; ?></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/site-header.php"; ?><main><section class="state-page"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/help/">Browse Programs</a><span>›</span><b>Maryland</b></div><div class="state-intro"><div><h1>Assistance Programs in Maryland</h1><p>11 programs, grouped by what you need help with. Each includes clear application guidance.</p></div><div><a class="button primary" href="/find/">Find my programs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><small>Free · Private · Takes under 2 minutes</small></div></div><section class="program-group"><h2>Rent &amp; Housing Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>211 Maryland</h3><p>Dial 2-1-1 from any Maryland phone for free, confidential help finding local assistance with housing, utilities, food, healthcare, and more. 211 Maryland is a statewide service that answers around the clock, every day of the year. You can also text your keyword to 898-211 for ongoing support, or search at 211md.org.</p><div><a href="/programs/211-maryland/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/211-maryland/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Maryland Legal Aid</h3><p>Maryland Legal Aid provides free civil legal help to low-income residents on housing and eviction, public benefits, family, consumer, and other noncriminal matters. Call the statewide intake line at 1-888-465-2468 to reach the office serving your area, or start an application online and find your local office at marylandlegalaid.org.</p><div><a href="/programs/maryland-legal-aid/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/maryland-legal-aid/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Maryland Medicaid (HealthChoice) &amp; MCHP</h3><p>Maryland Medicaid is free or low-cost health coverage for children, pregnant people, parents, older adults, people with disabilities, and low-income adults. Most members get care through HealthChoice, Maryland&#39;s Medicaid managed care program, and MCHP covers children through CHIP. Apply through Maryland Health Connection at marylandhealthconnection.gov, or call 1-855-642-8572, Monday through Friday, 8am to 6pm.</p><div><a href="/programs/maryland-medicaid-healthchoice-and-mchp/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/maryland-medicaid-healthchoice-and-mchp/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Weatherization Assistance Program (Maryland)</h3><p>Free home energy-efficiency work for income-eligible Maryland households: insulation, air sealing, and heating-system improvements that lower future bills. The Department of Housing and Community Development runs the program through local weatherization agencies. Contact the local agency serving your area to apply, or call 1-855-583-8976 for help finding it.</p><div><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-maryland/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-maryland/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Debt &amp; Credit Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Maryland Earned Income Tax Credit</h3><p>Maryland offers a state Earned Income Tax Credit on top of the federal credit, and part of it is refundable, so it can pay out even if you owe no tax. The nonrefundable state credit equals 50 percent of your federal EITC, and the refundable credit equals 45 percent of your federal EITC. Claim it on your Maryland return at marylandtaxes.gov.</p><div><a href="/programs/maryland-earned-income-tax-credit/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/maryland-earned-income-tax-credit/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Utility Bill Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Maryland Energy Assistance / Office of Home Energy Programs (OHEP)</h3><p>The Office of Home Energy Programs, OHEP, helps low-income Maryland households with home energy costs. It runs the Maryland Energy Assistance Program (MEAP) for heating grants, the Electric Universal Service Program (EUSP) for electric bills, and arrearage retirement help for past-due balances. Apply online through MarylandBenefits at MarylandBenefits.gov, at your local home energy program office, or by phone at 1-800-332-6347.</p><div><a href="/programs/maryland-energy-assistance-office-of-home-energy-programs-ohep/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/maryland-energy-assistance-office-of-home-energy-programs-ohep/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Maryland SNAP (Food Supplement Program)</h3><p>SNAP is Maryland&#39;s Food Supplement Program: monthly food money loaded onto an EBT card you use like a debit card at most grocery stores. Apply online through MarylandBenefits at MarylandBenefits.gov, which also handles Medicaid, cash assistance, and energy help on one account, or at your local department of social services. You can also call the DHS Customer Call Center at 1-800-332-6347, Monday through Friday, 8:30am to 5pm.</p><div><a href="/programs/maryland-snap-food-supplement-program/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/maryland-snap-food-supplement-program/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Cash Assistance &amp; Benefits</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Maryland Temporary Cash Assistance (TCA)</h3><p>Temporary Cash Assistance, TCA, is Maryland&#39;s monthly cash assistance for low-income families with children, and it is the state&#39;s version of the federal TANF program. Most adults take part in work activities while they receive it. Apply online through MarylandBenefits at MarylandBenefits.gov or at your local department of social services, or call 1-800-332-6347.</p><div><a href="/programs/maryland-temporary-cash-assistance-tca/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/maryland-temporary-cash-assistance-tca/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Unemployment Insurance (Maryland)</h3><p>Temporary weekly payments if you lost work through no fault of your own, from the Maryland Department of Labor. File online through the BEACON system at beacon.labor.maryland.gov, which is the fastest way, or call a claims agent at 667-207-6520, Monday through Friday, 8am to 4pm. You must certify each week to keep payments coming.</p><div><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-maryland/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-maryland/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Free &amp; Low-Cost Healthcare</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Maryland Temporary Disability Assistance Program (TDAP)</h3><p>TDAP is Maryland&#39;s monthly cash assistance for low-income adults with a disability who do not have dependent children. A licensed medical practitioner must verify the disability. Apply online through MarylandBenefits at MarylandBenefits.gov or at your local department of social services, or call 1-800-332-6347.</p><div><a href="/programs/maryland-temporary-disability-assistance-program-tdap/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/maryland-temporary-disability-assistance-program-tdap/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Food Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Maryland WIC</h3><p>WIC gives healthy food, breastfeeding support, nutrition education, and health referrals to pregnant and postpartum people, infants, and children up to age 5. Maryland WIC runs through local county offices of the Maryland Department of Health. Call 1-800-242-4942 to find your local clinic, or apply through the WIC Client Portal linked at health.maryland.gov/phpa/wic.</p><div><a href="/programs/maryland-wic/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/maryland-wic/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div></section></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="American Aid Network home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>AMERICAN <b>AID</b><small>NETWORK</small></span></a><p>Clear, reliable guidance to assistance programs across America.</p><div class="verified">✓ Information from trusted sources</div></div><div><h4>FIND SUPPORT</h4><a href="/find/">Find help near me</a><a href="/help/">Browse by state</a><a href="/programs/">Program guides</a><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a></div><div><h4>ABOUT</h4><a href="/about/">Our mission</a><a href="/legal/contact/">Contact us</a><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/legal/terms/">Terms of use</a></div></div><div class="wrap disclaimer">American Aid Network is an independent informational resource. We are not a government agency and do not administer benefit programs. Program details change; always confirm requirements with the official provider.<span>© 2026 American Aid Network</span></div></footer><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></body></html>